s a higher cost, but it is not a shut market.\n- **Capex size:** Pellham plans 2027 capex up 18% and Norvane up 12%, mostly substations and transformers.\n- **Equity:** Equity markets are weaker. Two utility share offerings were cut back in size. Pellham withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering because investor demand fell short.\n- **Effect on spending:** Pellham says it will cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and defer two substation programmes until financing improves. Debt alone is evidently not enough to fund its plan.\n\n**Gaps:** I found no data on issuance volumes, debt capacity, or credit metrics such as FFO/debt and ratings headroom. I can't say how much more debt the utilities could take on before it affects their ratings.\n\n**Conclusion:** Norvane, with the smaller increase, looks fundable through debt. Pellham is the constrained one. Expect 2027 capex to be partly deferred, which is negative for grid-equipment orders.\n\nSources: utility-capex-2027, utility-credit, pellham-offering.","ttft_ms":1467,"type":"result","duration_ms":18927,"uuid":"736bd1cc-bab2-441d-8ed7-b9f92f275467","ttft_stream_ms":834,"time_to_request_ms":73,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":8,"system_prompt":9,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":10,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":7,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":2,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":3,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":22,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":65,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":202,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":128,"process_rss_mib_result":198,"process_anon_mib_result":117,"process_peak_rss_mib":203,"process_cpu_ms_turn":494,"process_wall_ms_turn":18926,"process_cpu